The Gaggia Velasca Prestige is a coffee lover's dream machine. But can you use it with a drip coffee system?
No, the Gaggia Velasca Prestige is designed and built for espresso machines and should not be used with a drip coffee system. The machine uses a specific brewing method known as the "espresso method," which involves pushing a pressurized stream of hot water through finely ground coffee beans. This creates a concentrated shot of coffee, which can then be diluted with milk and other ingredients to make an espresso. This method is different from the drip coffee method, which involves slowly dripping hot water over coffee grounds in a filter basket. While some people have been known to use the Gaggia Velasca Prestige with a drip coffee system, this is not recommended and can damage the machine. If you want to use the Gaggia Velasca Prestige with a drip coffee system, you will have to disassemble the machine and use a separate drip coffee system to brew your morning coffee.
